From aef5e0d3b6a8c1e539a08eef0dccea681a30d33e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Input: stmfts - support the FTS8 generation

The controller on the Galaxy Tab A 10.1 (SM-T580) reports itself as an
ST FingerTipS part but does not answer the 0xa0 system reset command and
never raises the completion interrupt, so the driver fails to bring it
up.

It turns out to be a hybrid of two generations: the system reset is the
newer register write (0x28 0x80 through the 0xb6 window) while interrupt
enable is still the older 0x1c / 0x41 pair.  Neither vendor driver taken
whole would work; the combination only shows up when comparing them.
The newer 0x2c / 0x48 pair is worth calling out because it looks like it
works: the write is accepted and reads back, but nothing connects the
event FIFO to the attention output, so events queue up while the line
stays deasserted.  Both the register and the value are module parameters
so the pair can be checked from the command line on an unknown panel.

Bring-up therefore becomes: power cycle (avdd, 1 ms, vdd), warm boot CRC
check, system reset, then poll status 0x85 until CONTROLLER_READY while
tolerating spurious 0x0f events, and enable interrupts last.

The polling loops are bounded by a deadline rather than by a retry
count.  An unpowered controller pulls the bus down through its ESD
diodes and a single transfer then costs the adapter several seconds, at
which point a loop bounded at ten iterations still runs for minutes and
is indistinguishable from a hang.

Two more quirks on this part: the chip id at 0x04 reads back as zeroes
instead of the expected value, so the check is downgraded to a warning;
and reading the whole event FIFO in one transfer wedges the bus, so
events are read one at a time.  The power cycle needs
regulator_force_disable() because the rails come up already enabled.

Removal disables the attention output and sensing, so that the
controller is left in a state the next probe can start from.

Hover sensing and the LED are dropped: this generation does not
implement them.
